# Every harness CLI any workflow under .github/workflows/ installs, pinned once
# (`.tool-versions` format: one package and exactly one version per line). The
# npm ones are keyed by package name and pinned to an exact x.y.z; `goose` is
# Goose's vendor installer (bash and PowerShell), which takes GOOSE_VERSION;
# `cursor-agent` is Cursor's build id (YYYY.MM.DD-<hex>), which its installer
# cannot take, so scripts/install-cursor-agent.sh and scripts/cursor-installer.ps1
# pin the installer to it and it downloads that versioned package.
#
# Why every workflow: an unpinned install fails a passing tree whenever a
# publisher is mid-release (Copilot 1.0.115 shipped its package before its
# darwin-arm64 platform package and failed `check (macos-latest)`), and that is
# as true of the live e2e and explore workflows as of the required checks.
#
# scripts/check-harness-cli-pins.sh holds every workflow to this file. To move a
# pin: change it here, run the check, fix each workflow line it names, and let
# the PR's check jobs (scripts/verify-harness-cli-pins.sh, run on every OS when
# this file changes) prove each new version installs and reports itself.
